'''Oyda''' is an [[Afro-Asiatic languages|Afro-Asiatic]] language spoken in the [[Gamo Gofa Zone]] of [[Ethiopia]].<ref name=e18/>

The 2007 Census of Ethiopia<ref>{{cite web |url=http://www.csa.gov.et/ |title=Home |website=csa.gov.et}}</ref> lists 45,120 individuals for the ethnic group.

